      A 32-year-old female presents with a 2-week history of an exhausting, dry, hacking non-productive cough following an uncomplicated viral URI. Physical examination and chest radiograph are completely normal. She works as a high-school bus driver and requires an effective antitussive that does not cause central sedation, respiratory depression, or physical dependence, and has no structural or chemical relationship to opioid alkaloids.
