      <div class="correct-badge">Correct Answer: B</div>
      <div class="rationale">
        The right lung has two fissures: the oblique fissure and the horizontal fissure. The **horizontal fissure** separates the superior lobe from the middle lobe. Surface anatomically, it begins anteriorly at the **4th costal cartilage** (at the level of the right sternal border) and passes horizontally laterally around the chest wall to intersect the oblique fissure near the **5th rib (or 6th rib) in the midaxillary line**.
